Very important (about UPSERT keys)

Your dev said “upsert” (not MERGE). That usually means:

UPDATE ... WHERE <BusinessKey>

IF @@ROWCOUNT = 0 INSERT ...

In that pattern, the UPDATE statement does not always include RowID, and often RowID is not known.

✅ If their UPDATE does not set RowID, then this line in the update trigger:

JOIN st i ON tgt.RowID = i.RowID


can cause masking to be skipped or not apply.

Best solution

Change the join key to the same key they use in their upsert UPDATE (commonly ClassID + EnrolleeID, or EnrolleeID).

If you already know the key, tell me and I’ll rewrite the UPDATE trigger join line exactly.

For example (common):

JOIN st i
  ON tgt.ClassID = i.ClassID
 AND tgt.EnrolleeID = i.EnrolleeID

